1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,530
These AIs said most of
the job couldn't be done.

2
00:00:03,560 --> 00:00:05,010
Then they did it.

3
00:00:05,010 --> 00:00:07,330
Picture a famous building on paper.

4
00:00:07,330 --> 00:00:12,130
Now rebuild it brick by brick, while
a strict inspector checks every brick.

5
00:00:12,130 --> 00:00:14,400
The building is a famous math proof.

6
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:18,350
Fermat scribbled the rule
in a book's margin in 1637.

7
00:00:18,350 --> 00:00:21,760
Proving it took 358 years.

8
00:00:21,760 --> 00:00:23,880
But paper can hide mistakes.

9
00:00:23,880 --> 00:00:25,940
In a computer language called Lean,

10
00:00:25,940 --> 00:00:29,300
the inspector is a machine,
and nothing gets past it.

11
00:00:29,300 --> 00:00:32,600
In September, Claude agents
did it for the first time.

12
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:37,110
13 million lines, a researcher
guiding them, 11 days.

13
00:00:37,110 --> 00:00:41,080
This week, Anthropic tried
again with Claude Fable 5.2.

14
00:00:41,080 --> 00:00:43,600
1,000 copies, no researcher.

15
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:47,060
One boss and 999 helpers.

16
00:00:47,060 --> 00:00:47,980
The twist?

17
00:00:47,980 --> 00:00:51,350
The helpers looked at 60
sections and said 47 couldn't

18
00:00:51,350 --> 00:00:52,530
be done in time.

19
00:00:52,530 --> 00:00:56,100
The boss set those aside and put
nearly everyone on the other 10.

20
00:00:56,100 --> 00:00:57,970
Done in about 70 minutes.

21
00:00:57,970 --> 00:01:00,940
Then the boss wrote: "There
is no reason to idle."

22
00:01:00,940 --> 00:01:03,100
And sent the helpers
back to the hard ones.

23
00:01:03,100 --> 00:01:07,030
Less than 30 hours later, the
whole proof passed the inspector.

24
00:01:07,030 --> 00:01:07,970
The catch?

25
00:01:07,970 --> 00:01:10,080
Humans designed this building long ago,

26
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:12,780
and the team had a head
start: 60 checkpoints,

27
00:01:12,780 --> 00:01:16,150
a one-line map, 47 bricks already laid.

28
00:01:16,150 --> 00:01:17,470
Anthropic's lesson?

29
00:01:17,470 --> 00:01:20,150
Agents give up on hard problems too early.

30
00:01:20,150 --> 00:01:23,800
Even this boss got 19 automatic
reminders to keep going.

31
00:01:23,800 --> 00:01:26,360
So when an AI says
something can't be done,

32
00:01:26,360 --> 00:01:27,750
tell it to keep going.

33
00:01:27,750 --> 00:01:30,790
There's one word in this
video I never said out loud.

34
00:01:30,790 --> 00:01:31,620
Spotted it?

35
00:01:31,620 --> 00:01:32,460
Comment it.

36
00:01:32,460 --> 00:01:35,520
Follow for more AI, explained like this.
